{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/19600-no-warfare-guild","id":19600,"title":"No Warfare guild?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-28T00:42:53-08:00","id":19600,"title":"No Warfare guild?","content":"Something I just realized. We have Alchemists, Middle Managers, Embalmers, Judges/paper pushers, and Engineers. <br /> <br /> But no guild dedicated to warfare. I find it odd that a massively powerful civilization that wants to horde all relics to the end of time seem to left off the most important profession that deals with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T00:55:45-08:00","id":19605,"title":"","content":"No this was something that bothered me when I read the book, wondering first if the Deceived were going to be the War guild, but hey were Artists. I guess though since every legion has two Shan'iatu assigned tall the guilds I guess had an army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T02:54:37-08:00","id":19634,"title":"","content":"You would think it was part of the plan of the Shan'Iatu to give people with military training immortality for all eternity.<br /> <br /> Oh, wait.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T07:36:30-08:00","id":19725,"title":"","content":"So, my understanding was that the Shan'Iatu created the arisen, from the start, to be their earthly servants for after they completed their great work, and sank Irem into Duat.<br /> The Shan'Iatu plan ahead.<br /> They needed skilled workers to find and manage sources of Sekhem.<br /> What they didn't care about was conquering the LIVING world anymore. Who cares about the living world? We have DUAT to conquer!<br /> So, what they left behind, and made ever living, were servants and slaves who were best suited for their purpose (gather magic shit and send it to us in Duat).<br /> The Generals? The Warriors? They took those with them into Duat. Because if you want to overthrow nameless eternal Gods in their own timeless and immortal realm, you BETTER have a good army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T15:17:35-08:00","id":19916,"title":"","content":"So far, ive found warriors can fit neatly into various guilds. Organizer-leiutenant and military quartermasters would be Maa-kep. Glorious warriors and &quot;martial artists&quot; wouldve been Deceived. Artillery, tech, and training could be Mesen-Nebu. Lawkeepers and couriers would be Sesha-Hebsu. Tacticians and logistics would be Tef-aabi. Deathbringers and templar would be su-menent. Though, the bulk of irem's army was slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T22:17:37-08:00","id":20508,"title":"","content":"The deathless are emphatically middle-class. Historically, soldiers? Not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T23:04:24-08:00","id":20514,"title":"","content":"There are some warriors and guardians in the Guilds as presented, but really the core of it is that the Arisen come from groups of artisans and scholars. While Lost Irem had armies, as I understand it they were far removed from the guilds of old. You might find a legbreaker here or a temple guardian there, but the vast majority were intelligent skilled workers who practiced a trade.<br /> <br /> I'm not all that attached to the idea, but unless I missed something big the particular niches that the Arisen came from in life were a very intentional part of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T23:50:12-08:00","id":20521,"title":"","content":"Traditionally you don't want to make your soldiers immortal and imbue them with phenomenal cosmic powers.<br /> <br /> Even a little power has been known to start uprisings, one of the sample relics, the Jackal's Hunger, was made from the blood of a general who decided that if the Nameless Empire would not let him join the ranks of the Shan'iatu, he would force them to.<br /> <br /> An entire guild of immortal super soldiers? That would be just asking for trouble. For every Steve Rogers you'll get two Frank Simpsons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-30-2013, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T02:22:15-08:00","id":20559,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you'd really get a lot of professional soldiers in this era. I'd expect the nobles of Irem to be providing military leadership, presumably with the Pharaoh at the front, with the footsoliders made up of conscripts from the general population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T11:28:54-08:00","id":22460,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and the few &quot;professional/artisan&quot; warriors could be modelled after one of the guilds' philosophies. it isn't terribly much of a stretch to imagine a tef'aabhi designing military formations, or an alchemist measuring the dedwen of his blade and skill with it in converting alive to dead, and deaths into losses of power. none of these will be simple soldiers--theyd be artists and influential warriors, who led/were worth many slave-soldiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}